# UniWeb Owner hard rules (permanent — 2026-08-15)

Owner communication stays simple Hindi/Urdu; product UI English. Local laptop only.

## Never build / never restore

- **NBFC product** — no lending, no NBFC menus, no `merchant_nbfc*`, no `admin_nbfc`, no `includes/nbfc.php`. Do not re-add.
- **Customer PPI wallet** — no `customer_wallet.php`, no consumer prepaid balance. Merchant `wallet.php` = settlement balance only (keep).
- **White-label program / product** — UniWeb does **not** sell white-label (no reseller portal, no `*_v2` branded app, no “buy white-label” sales). Do not build or market one.

## Partner program vs white-label (hard)

- **Partner program = yes.** UniWeb works **with** bank / PG / KYC partners (keys, registry, forwards). Keep and fix that existing flow.
- **White-label program = no.** Partners are not sold a full rebranded UniWeb.
- **Merchant branding limit (only this):**
  1. Merchant may **add / use their own domain** (same site — Hostinger / existing domain flow; not a second app).
  2. Merchant may **customize checkout** (`checkout_customize.php` — logo, colours, titles).
- Nothing beyond those two for “looks like my brand.” Do not invent full portal white-label.

## Existing-first (hard)

- **Do not invent new features / new product pages** for “nice to have” or market parity.
- Work **only on pages and features that already exist** (fix, wire, clean, search, decrypt, nav).
- **Create a new page/file only if** the Owner-approved gap has **no existing page** and the work cannot be done by editing an existing one.
- PDF audit points = fix existing wiring/bugs/copy/search — not a licence to add Route, orchestrator, POS, white-label shell, or second apps.
- Phase 10 `WHITE_LABEL_CHECKLIST.md` = **reference only** (deal ops), never a product launch.

## Still parked unless Owner says start

- Live Route / Split SDK (Phase 11).
- Partner live keys = Owner pastes in UI.
- Do not DROP production DB.
